              "id": "V5erNC",
              "name": "Path note",
              "fill": "$ui:color-text-secondary",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1100,
              "content": "Ownership is a set, not a checkbox, and it can never fall to zero. A member can make another member an owner, step back once somebody else owns it, and take an account out of wimm altogether — which is reversible and is what they were reaching for when they used to disown their last one. Every state here is the same screen: Who sees these accounts, reached from the household's accounts at any time.",
              "lineHeight": 1.45,
              "fontFamily": "$ui:type-family-body",
